"},{"id":"12dddc64eaed","b":"MRK","v":"npnf.hilarius.de_synodis","w":"hilarius.de_synodis","a":"hilarius_von_poitiers","s":1,"p":[170,170],"r":[13,32],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mark xiii. 32."},{"id":"530aca4a73ab","b":"1PE","v":"npnf.hilarius.de_synodis","w":"hilarius.de_synodis","a":"hilarius_von_poitiers","s":1,"p":[170,170],"r":[3,20],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mehtuselah's age was a favourite problem with the early Church. See Aug. de Civ. Dei, xv. 13, and de pexx. orig. ii. 23, where it is said to be one of those points on which a Christian can afford to be ignorant. According to the septuagint, Methuselah lived for fourteen years after the deluge, so that more than `eitht souls 0'' survived, and 1 Pet. iii. 20 appreared to be incorrect. According to the Hebrew and Vullgate there is not difficulty, as Methuselah is represented as dying before the deluge."},{"id":"a96d5be9a04f","b":"HEB","v":"npnf.hilarius.de_synodis","w":"hilarius.de_synodis","a":"hilarius_von_poitiers","s":1,"p":[170,170],"r":[5,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Heb. v. 12."}]}
